1
00:00:49,040 --> 00:02:02,000
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:02:02,510 --> 00:02:06,750
NO ANIMALS WERE HARMED DURING
THE FILMING OF THIS PRODUCTION.

3
00:02:11,710 --> 00:02:13,560
Men!

4
00:02:14,090 --> 00:02:18,740
Blaming each other will not make our job
any easier.

5
00:02:19,290 --> 00:02:22,260
The importance of listening to Osman is
obvious.

6
00:02:22,690 --> 00:02:27,740
A governor is killed, the one who was
blamed is a Tent's commander's son.

7
00:02:28,840 --> 00:02:35,110
Remember, there is Byzantine on one side,
Seljuk on the other.

8
00:02:35,680 --> 00:02:40,350
Because of this, I say we establish a
fair court in Söğüt inn tomorrow.

9
00:02:40,570 --> 00:02:42,850
Why in Söğüt, and not Kulucahisar?

10
00:02:43,770 --> 00:02:48,460
Osman committed the majority of the
crimes mentioned in Kulucahisar.

11
00:02:50,060 --> 00:02:52,380
We should be the judges.

12
00:02:52,380 --> 00:02:57,580
What matters isn't trial, it's
finding out what the truth is, Kalonoz.

13
00:02:57,750 --> 00:03:04,990
Besides, will any of the Beys, Tents agree with
the decision you'll make in Kulucahisar?

14
00:03:06,490 --> 00:03:09,230
Alişar Bey is right, Kalonoz.

15
00:03:12,180 --> 00:03:18,300
Osman should stand trial in Söğüt so that
no question goes unanswered.

16
00:03:19,350 --> 00:03:23,920
A court established under the guidance
of our fair judges...

17
00:03:24,610 --> 00:03:28,160
... is the most beneficial for all of us.

18
00:03:28,160 --> 00:03:30,800
We also agree with this.

19
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:36,330
As long as our relationship with my
deceased friend Yorgopolos...

20
00:03:36,330 --> 00:03:40,120
... which is on the verge of war,
is rebuilt.

21
00:03:41,850 --> 00:03:46,790
Let's not shed blood for the reasons
of insignificance.

22
00:03:48,670 --> 00:03:50,950
Osman is a fugitive now.

23
00:03:50,950 --> 00:03:54,610
You couldn't even keep him in the
cage in your own Tent.

24
00:03:54,610 --> 00:03:56,570
What if he doesn't show up in Söğüt inn?

25
00:03:56,570 --> 00:04:00,550
Then, including the murder of
the governor...

26
00:04:02,330 --> 00:04:05,500
... he will have accepted all of
the offences.

27
00:04:45,610 --> 00:04:49,360
I'm sure Osman Bey will be at the court.

28
00:04:49,360 --> 00:04:51,570
Rest assured.

29
00:04:52,300 --> 00:04:55,980
His own uncle couldn't keep him in
his own hands.

30
00:04:55,980 --> 00:04:58,950
How can you be so sure?

31
00:05:01,270 --> 00:05:06,140
The Turkmens in these lands are like
mad horses, Sofia.

32
00:05:07,270 --> 00:05:12,690
Everyone has a different head collar, but
each head collar is tied to the same pole.

33
00:05:14,210 --> 00:05:18,210
I am that pole itself.

34
00:05:19,380 --> 00:05:24,740
A person in the Turkish Tents with words
more powerful than mine...

35
00:05:24,740 --> 00:05:28,470
... is not yet born.

36
00:05:29,740 --> 00:05:33,910
If Osman doesn't come alive...

37
00:05:33,910 --> 00:05:35,930
... his corpse will.

38
00:05:35,930 --> 00:05:39,720
This is the word of the Banner Lord
Alişar Bey.

39
00:05:40,650 --> 00:05:45,740
Since you are this confident in
your words, as allies...

40
00:05:46,260 --> 00:05:50,120
... our part is to trust your word.

41
00:05:59,690 --> 00:06:03,280
We'll be waiting for the news, Alişar Bey.

42
00:06:05,050 --> 00:06:08,560
The truth will come to light tomorrow.

43
00:06:08,670 --> 00:06:14,160
Let's hope for the best for all of us.

44
00:06:56,680 --> 00:06:59,240
Who are they, my Osman?

45
00:06:59,240 --> 00:07:01,280
No need, Bamsı Bey.

46
00:07:03,170 --> 00:07:06,390
- Where is Edebali?
- He sent me.

47
00:07:06,960 --> 00:07:09,980
- My name is Zülfikar.
- We shall go to him swiftly.

48
00:07:09,990 --> 00:07:14,590
- Bamsı Bey, you take the lead here.
- Thank you, Osman. Thank you.

49
00:07:34,710 --> 00:07:39,220
Alişar Bey is giving a helping
hand, you saw it.

50
00:07:39,220 --> 00:07:44,600
He isn't holding Osman at arm's length,
that's why he's moving the court to Söğüt.

51
00:07:46,500 --> 00:07:51,420
Alişar Bey is preparing the wolf's
dining table, my nephew.

52
00:07:51,430 --> 00:07:56,690
He wants those who are out of
breath to die.

53
00:07:57,720 --> 00:08:01,790
It's true that he is giving a helping
hand. But...

54
00:08:01,800 --> 00:08:10,360
... we'll find it out together whether if
this hand will help us or strangle us.

55
00:08:12,600 --> 00:08:16,600
What if the court's decision is
against Osman, uncle?

56
00:08:17,690 --> 00:08:23,670
- Will we sacrifice my brother?
- We need to find Osman first.

57
00:08:24,600 --> 00:08:29,910
We need to submit evidence which will
convince the court that Osman is innocent.

58
00:08:30,610 --> 00:08:37,500
Then I will make him pay for what
he did to Batur.

59
00:08:38,800 --> 00:08:43,800
Osman is my blood, my life.

60
00:08:44,830 --> 00:08:48,640
Only I can punish him.

61
00:08:56,190 --> 00:08:58,110
I hope nothing's wrong.

62
00:09:20,040 --> 00:09:22,410
Osman's Alps. (Men)

63
00:09:31,490 --> 00:09:33,540
So you're here.

64
00:09:34,390 --> 00:09:36,970
Boğaç brother, take Tursun to the
nursing tent.

65
00:09:36,970 --> 00:09:38,380
Very well, brother.

66
00:09:38,380 --> 00:09:41,840
And we'll take Bala Hatun to
Ertuğrul Bey's pavilion, come on!

67
00:09:42,340 --> 00:09:44,560
They are injured, uncle.

68
00:09:58,820 --> 00:10:00,720
Boran Alp!

69
00:10:16,050 --> 00:10:21,130
All rivers fall into the sea.

70
00:10:22,410 --> 00:10:24,220
We're not here to stay, Dündar Bey.

71
00:10:24,220 --> 00:10:29,530
I decide who stays and who leaves
in this Tent.

72
00:10:34,210 --> 00:10:35,890
Who is this Hatun?

73
00:10:37,490 --> 00:10:40,540
Sheikh Edebali's daughter Bala Hatun.

74
00:10:47,280 --> 00:10:50,630
The Hatun who was kidnapped from
the bazaar was Edebali's daughter?

75
00:10:51,260 --> 00:10:52,910
That's right.

76
00:10:58,890 --> 00:11:02,830
Having her as a guest is my Bey's order.

77
00:11:03,240 --> 00:11:08,440
Why did your Bey send the Hatun with you?
Was he not brave enough?

78
00:11:08,440 --> 00:11:11,940
My Bey's bravery can neither be contained
in this Tent nor in these lands.

79
00:11:11,940 --> 00:11:16,980
It's against Kayı laws to make a Muslim
woman in need of help wait.

80
00:11:17,990 --> 00:11:24,000
We'd wreck the whole world for
a drop of Muslim blood.

81
00:11:24,650 --> 00:11:28,590
Tell Zöhre Hatun to take care of
her quickly.

82
00:11:28,920 --> 00:11:33,310
Edebali's daughter is also our daughter.

83
00:11:34,930 --> 00:11:37,630
Come on, take her.

84
00:12:15,390 --> 00:12:19,010
- Peace be with you.
- Peace be with you too.

85
00:12:19,610 --> 00:12:22,880
Zülfikar Dervish told us that you were
aware of the situation.

86
00:12:32,070 --> 00:12:35,380
Bala Hatun is on the verge of death.

87
00:12:36,630 --> 00:12:38,920
What are you looking for here?

88
00:12:44,030 --> 00:12:47,940
Batur, take Osman's Alps to the cage.

89
00:12:47,940 --> 00:12:51,710
Don't let them go anywhere until
Osman comes here.

90
00:12:53,870 --> 00:12:58,080
Dündar Bey, you're stoking the fire.

91
00:13:00,220 --> 00:13:04,280
The fire is not yet ignited Boran Alp.

92
00:13:05,690 --> 00:13:07,570
It's not yet ignited.

93
00:13:07,570 --> 00:13:10,880
Your wish is my command, my Bey.

94
00:13:37,090 --> 00:13:41,760
At last, we have a valuable clay.

95
00:13:43,710 --> 00:13:46,730
It was worth it after all, huh Zülfikar?

96
00:13:46,730 --> 00:13:48,480
Thanks to you, master.

97
00:13:51,670 --> 00:13:55,960
It's not the time to dig around Edebali.
We don't have time.

98
00:14:01,140 --> 00:14:06,020
It's not easy, son. It's not easy.

99
00:14:10,490 --> 00:14:15,670
Neither finding nor existing.
It's not easy.

100
00:14:19,660 --> 00:14:22,390
Making a pot of mystery isn't easy, son.

101
00:14:22,390 --> 00:14:26,090
First, labour. Then patience.

102
00:14:26,090 --> 00:14:31,080
First, light from your eyes, then sweat
from your forehead.

103
00:14:31,830 --> 00:14:38,240
First you get some mud.
Then you seperate the clay from the rock.

104
00:14:41,390 --> 00:14:46,910
Stronger the clay, more durable the pot.

105
00:14:48,140 --> 00:14:50,470
Bala Hatun is fighting for her life in
the Tent.

106
00:14:50,470 --> 00:14:55,340
For this reason, its story is
similar to a human's.

107
00:14:55,340 --> 00:14:59,410
Just like how a pot of mystery
is made from dirt...

108
00:14:59,410 --> 00:15:02,350
... humans were created from dirt.

109
00:15:06,470 --> 00:15:10,850
If its master is capable, and its
core is beautiful...

110
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:14,660
Both can be shaped easily.

111
00:15:21,330 --> 00:15:24,070
Humans are also like this, Osman Bey.

112
00:15:25,220 --> 00:15:29,880
They're raw, they burn, they cook.

113
00:15:31,020 --> 00:15:36,760
If it's clay is defective, effort is
low, and the fire is small...

114
00:15:36,780 --> 00:15:39,030
The pot of mystery cracks.

115
00:15:39,030 --> 00:15:40,990
Water begins to leak

116
00:15:42,300 --> 00:15:46,300
Just like how Adam was raw.

117
00:15:47,530 --> 00:15:54,180
Fire makes dirt a pot, patience makes
a human mature, son.

118
00:15:56,800 --> 00:16:00,300
A pot of mystery or a human.
What's the difference?

119
00:16:03,060 --> 00:16:07,310
For this reason, if my daughter Bala faces
such hardships...

120
00:16:07,900 --> 00:16:12,880
... overcomes such challenges, stands
against such difficulties...

121
00:16:14,070 --> 00:16:18,350
... then she is the rewarded one.
She is the winner.

122
00:16:22,120 --> 00:16:28,770
So what, just because she was Edebali's
daughter, she wouldn't be tested?

123
00:16:31,290 --> 00:16:37,040
In doomsday, the day in which no one
can help one another...

124
00:16:37,660 --> 00:16:41,050
... what would we do, my little Osman?

125
00:16:45,220 --> 00:16:52,160
Didn't our prophet say, "I won't be
able to help my daughter Fatma that day."?

126
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:31,510
She has a low pulse.

127
00:17:40,740 --> 00:17:45,280
She is poisoned. We can't do anything.

128
00:17:47,230 --> 00:17:49,180
She will die.

129
00:17:49,330 --> 00:17:52,410
Osman trusted me with her.

130
00:17:52,410 --> 00:18:00,090
This is Hayma Ana's pavilion. You don't
reject someone in need of healing here.

131
00:18:06,040 --> 00:18:09,350
Let's boil some castor oil. We need to
make her puke.

132
00:18:16,420 --> 00:18:18,650
Boil castor oil.

133
00:18:28,010 --> 00:18:30,110
Give me a rag.

134
00:18:30,840 --> 00:18:35,130
Now little Osman. Tell me what's
bothering you.

135
00:18:35,450 --> 00:18:38,470
They wanted to make you pay.

136
00:18:40,300 --> 00:18:43,060
They want the treasure.

137
00:18:44,040 --> 00:18:46,750
If you don't give it to them...

138
00:18:48,740 --> 00:18:51,980
... your daughter Bala...

139
00:18:51,980 --> 00:18:54,670
... will shortly die.

140
00:18:56,210 --> 00:18:59,520
Sons of the devil.

141
00:18:59,530 --> 00:19:03,400
They still think death comes
from the poison.

142
00:19:03,950 --> 00:19:07,890
This arrogance of the little devils...

143
00:19:08,660 --> 00:19:12,160
This devil didn't submit to Adam either.

144
00:19:14,680 --> 00:19:21,020
As long as Allah doesn't allow for it, so
what if they make her drink thousands...

145
00:19:21,020 --> 00:19:23,410
... of poisons, so what if my child dies?

146
00:19:24,910 --> 00:19:30,090
We'll be happy that she'll be our
prophet's neighbour in the afterlife.

147
00:19:34,120 --> 00:19:36,490
You're right.

148
00:19:36,490 --> 00:19:41,350
The ones who don't know about sacrifices,
the ones who can't say goodbye...

149
00:19:41,350 --> 00:19:46,210
... who can't accept being a mortal,
shall not desire anything.

150
00:19:46,210 --> 00:19:51,630
Is it easy to stand before Allah as
a Muslim, little Osman?

151
00:19:53,210 --> 00:19:56,800
A Muslim must be honourable.

152
00:19:57,330 --> 00:20:04,940
Honourable ones are those who don't forget
the truth at the times of hardships.

153
00:20:05,650 --> 00:20:08,830
So are we going to stay here and
do nothing?

154
00:20:09,330 --> 00:20:13,300
- Sofia is Yannis' daughter.
- Yannis' daughter?

155
00:20:13,300 --> 00:20:18,160
Let's see what Yannis will do
when you capture her.

156
00:20:21,190 --> 00:20:25,770
Me capturing Sofia, how do you know these?

157
00:20:26,200 --> 00:20:32,390
We spent our lives digging the proper
clay from the dirt, son.

158
00:20:32,390 --> 00:20:37,450
Our eyes can see a proper man.

159
00:20:39,020 --> 00:20:42,540
Now I'll go to your Tent as a guest.

160
00:20:42,540 --> 00:20:46,610
If you bring the antitoxin, good.

161
00:20:46,610 --> 00:20:50,590
If you can't, don't you blame yourself.

162
00:20:52,370 --> 00:20:56,780
Our cause is having the consciousness
of an ant.

163
00:20:58,420 --> 00:21:01,270
We just want where we stand to be known.

164
00:21:04,390 --> 00:21:08,180
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim
(In the name of Allah, the compassionate, the merciful)

165
00:21:09,500 --> 00:21:13,520
You're right, Edebali. What is so
important about this treasure?

166
00:21:13,520 --> 00:21:17,890
It's a piece of wood, son.
A piece of wood.

167
00:21:20,210 --> 00:21:22,900
I'd like to hear about it one day.

168
00:21:22,900 --> 00:21:27,910
- I need to go now.
- Always be on the right path, son.

169
00:21:28,270 --> 00:21:30,980
I bid you farewell.

170
00:22:00,470 --> 00:22:06,010
- Aslı and Kerem.
- I worked hard on it. It's finally done.

171
00:22:23,410 --> 00:22:27,500
Open your eyes, Aygül.
Her corpse is in the pavilion.

172
00:22:27,500 --> 00:22:30,120
Think about where her soul is.

173
00:22:50,090 --> 00:22:52,770
Look what's written here, Sofia.

174
00:22:54,160 --> 00:22:58,390
A verse from the Surah Al-Hujurat
in Quran.

175
00:23:00,690 --> 00:23:06,290
"The believers are but brothers".
Surah Al-Hujurat [49:10]

176
00:23:09,850 --> 00:23:15,970
Quran calls them for unity
and solidarity 82 times.

177
00:23:17,670 --> 00:23:22,350
This is our starting point, Sofia.

178
00:23:23,710 --> 00:23:27,500
A great fire of disorder to be ignited.

179
00:23:30,730 --> 00:23:35,020
Now I'm listening to you. What news did
you bring from the Kayı Tent?

180
00:23:36,240 --> 00:23:41,640
Kayı Tent is boiling, master.
Dündar is very angry towards Osman.

181
00:23:43,080 --> 00:23:49,080
We can use that anger.
Because Osman ignores Dündar as a Bey.

182
00:23:49,540 --> 00:23:53,800
Dündar might be a Bey.
But in Kayı Tent...

183
00:23:53,800 --> 00:23:57,790
... Ertuğrul's son Osman's soul
is wandering about.

184
00:23:58,350 --> 00:24:00,790
I can feel it, Sofia.

185
00:24:00,790 --> 00:24:05,140
Now only for us, Osman will also
cause trouble for Dündar.

186
00:24:06,770 --> 00:24:12,200
This fire we worked up, will take us
to the treasure.

187
00:24:12,500 --> 00:24:16,230
Do you think Osman knows
where the treasure is?

188
00:24:16,230 --> 00:24:19,750
It's impossible for Osman to know where
the treasure is.

189
00:24:20,830 --> 00:24:26,340
Edebali won't ever tell Ahis' secrets
to Osman.

190
00:24:26,340 --> 00:24:30,330
He's so in love with that girl that he'd
oppose even Edebali.

191
00:24:32,750 --> 00:24:36,010
You'll see. He'll bring us the treasure.

192
00:24:46,970 --> 00:24:50,300
Master Yannis. There are news
from Nizamettin.

193
00:24:50,300 --> 00:24:55,080
- Tell me, Helen.
- Osman has sent Bala Hatun to Kayı Tent.

194
00:25:00,210 --> 00:25:02,090
Love.

195
00:25:03,500 --> 00:25:07,720
I bow to you one more time.

196
00:25:11,590 --> 00:25:16,300
I witnessed love's power when
I killed the governor.

197
00:25:19,410 --> 00:25:24,360
But Osman...
We can't be sure what he'll do.

198
00:25:25,220 --> 00:25:29,430
You can be sure that he'll bring
Ahis' treasure, Kalonoz.

199
00:25:29,430 --> 00:25:34,670
The love in him, his hatred toward me...

200
00:25:34,670 --> 00:25:38,130
... will bring me the treasure
sooner or later.

201
00:25:40,300 --> 00:25:45,050
And when he comes, we will
have taken our precautions.

202
00:26:07,780 --> 00:26:09,860
Alişar Bey.

203
00:26:13,460 --> 00:26:19,120
Do you know what the fish and humans have
in common, Nizamettin?

204
00:26:22,500 --> 00:26:28,100
Both get in trouble if they open
their mouth unnecessarily.

205
00:26:34,170 --> 00:26:37,750
Now, spill the beans.

206
00:26:40,160 --> 00:26:46,440
My Bey, it's my greatest honour to be your
eyes and ears, you know that.

207
00:26:47,220 --> 00:26:51,910
- I couldn't keep it, I brought it to you.
- I don't like empty words.

208
00:26:53,040 --> 00:26:56,310
Don't sugarcoat it, tell me quickly!

209
00:26:58,010 --> 00:27:02,010
Sheikh Edebali's daughter Bala Hatun
was poisoned.

210
00:27:03,120 --> 00:27:05,620
They took her to Kayı Tent.

211
00:27:07,390 --> 00:27:09,980
What are they up to?

212
00:27:12,850 --> 00:27:18,950
My Bey, more importantly, Osman is with
Sergeant Samsa.

213
00:27:18,950 --> 00:27:22,290
Most probably Sheikh Edebali is also
with them.

214
00:27:42,350 --> 00:27:46,730
So Edebali is the one who fans
Osman's flame.

215
00:27:51,490 --> 00:27:58,490
We shall put that fire out so that our
words are not in vain.

216
00:28:03,710 --> 00:28:10,560
Now go find Osman. Tell him, Alişar Bey
is calling you to the court.

217
00:28:11,500 --> 00:28:14,000
What if he doesn't want to come, my Bey?

218
00:28:14,620 --> 00:28:18,570
He will. He promised me.

219
00:28:21,640 --> 00:28:26,790
If he doesn't come, I'll rip
his heart out.

220
00:28:27,780 --> 00:28:32,140
I'll blunt that sword of his.

221
00:28:40,880 --> 00:28:44,930
Osman is on fire, my Bey.
What if he does something to Nizamettin?

222
00:28:49,540 --> 00:28:55,510
To feed the fish, you have to
sacrifice the bread, Zorba.

223
00:29:11,270 --> 00:29:13,620
My father...

224
00:29:14,600 --> 00:29:18,730
... took your Alp status. If it was me,
I would have taken your lives.

225
00:29:20,200 --> 00:29:23,980
If you were a fire, you'd burn a
place of your size, Batur.

226
00:29:24,910 --> 00:29:28,710
For Osman Bey's cause, we are honoured if
our Alp status is taken...

227
00:29:28,710 --> 00:29:30,700
... or our lives are taken.

228
00:29:31,280 --> 00:29:35,280
It will be your Bey Osman's
turn eventually.

229
00:29:43,190 --> 00:29:46,480
If you're any brave untie my hands.

230
00:29:47,060 --> 00:29:50,650
- Untie them!
- I will.

231
00:29:51,940 --> 00:29:58,570
I will but first, you all will see
what punishment is!

232
00:29:58,840 --> 00:30:03,760
You all will see what punishment is!
You all will see!

233
00:30:04,010 --> 00:30:08,850
Every single one of you will know what
a punishment is!

234
00:30:18,190 --> 00:30:23,400
So, we kissed your hand, we split your
bread with our own hands.

235
00:30:23,400 --> 00:30:25,660
Won't you help yourself, Konur brother?

236
00:30:28,230 --> 00:30:33,310
We kissed each other's hands, we took
the edge off...

237
00:30:35,350 --> 00:30:39,350
From now on even the grass we step on
will heal us.

238
00:30:40,230 --> 00:30:44,230
- Yes, Sergeant Samsa.
- Thank you.

239
00:30:45,890 --> 00:30:50,730
Such trees rumble with their leaves.

240
00:30:51,550 --> 00:30:55,030
- Wonderful, wonderful!
- May we come in, Osman Bey?

241
00:30:55,030 --> 00:30:57,110
Come in, Çetin Alp.

242
00:31:00,750 --> 00:31:03,850
My Bey, ruler of the New Bazaar
Nizamettin is here.

243
00:31:03,850 --> 00:31:06,570
He has something to tell you if you
please.

244
00:31:08,850 --> 00:31:12,850
Let him come in. Let's see what he wants.

245
00:31:25,450 --> 00:31:28,140
They are looking for me everywhere.

246
00:31:29,090 --> 00:31:32,770
Where did you hear about it Nizamettin?

247
00:31:35,860 --> 00:31:40,330
As you know Osman Bey, knowledge
is more valuable than coin.

248
00:31:41,460 --> 00:31:45,240
You must have eyes and ears everywhere,
so that you can know.

249
00:31:46,720 --> 00:31:52,160
Keep your eyes open. You might be
blinded one day.

250
00:31:52,690 --> 00:31:55,010
You might go deaf.

251
00:32:05,800 --> 00:32:09,800
Shall I cut his ears and put his eyes out
so he can no longer work, Osman Bey?

252
00:32:19,930 --> 00:32:22,360
Let him go, Sergeant Samsa.

253
00:32:28,230 --> 00:32:32,950
Tell me. What brings you here?

254
00:32:38,160 --> 00:32:42,670
Alişar Bey wants you to come up to court
and stand trial.

255
00:32:43,110 --> 00:32:46,990
He wants it so the real killers can
come to light.

256
00:32:47,890 --> 00:32:53,720
He wants it so you can go hunting
together like in the old days.

257
00:33:11,400 --> 00:33:15,900
Say hello to Alişar Bey for us.
He shall feel at ease.

258
00:33:17,080 --> 00:33:20,270
Everything will come to light tomorrow.

259
00:33:41,120 --> 00:33:45,150
Hatun. What's the state of Bala Hatun?

260
00:33:45,150 --> 00:33:49,790
It's not good, Gündüz Bey.
They poisoned her.

261
00:33:50,900 --> 00:33:55,490
If we can't find a cure, I don't know
if she will see another day.

262
00:33:57,180 --> 00:34:00,680
- May I come in, my Bey?
- Come in, Kılıç Alp.

263
00:34:05,240 --> 00:34:08,470
My Bey, Sheikh Edebali is here.

264
00:34:08,470 --> 00:34:11,340
Don't make him wait, let him come in.

265
00:34:23,880 --> 00:34:27,770
- Peace be with you.
- Peace be with you too.

266
00:34:27,770 --> 00:34:31,930
You have honoured Ertuğrul Gazi's
pavilion, Edebali. Welcome.

267
00:34:31,930 --> 00:34:34,570
Thank you.

268
00:34:34,570 --> 00:34:38,510
We're welcomed, son. Is Bala Hatun inside?

269
00:34:38,510 --> 00:34:41,820
Gonca Hatun is with her. She is resting.

270
00:34:41,820 --> 00:34:46,310
If you allow me, I want to see
my daughter.

271
00:34:46,310 --> 00:34:48,450
Not at all!

272
00:34:50,710 --> 00:34:54,710
Osman stepped on our laws, he stepped
on you.

273
00:34:55,800 --> 00:34:59,450
Give Osman the punishment he deserves.

274
00:35:01,780 --> 00:35:07,450
Osman not only threatens your
prosperity, your pavilion, our son...

275
00:35:07,920 --> 00:35:10,140
... but also Aygül.

276
00:35:10,750 --> 00:35:13,010
What are you trying to say, Hatun?

277
00:35:13,970 --> 00:35:20,050
My Bey... Aygül is in love with
Osman, my Bey.

278
00:35:25,040 --> 00:35:27,540
Osman doesn't feel anything towards Aygül.

279
00:35:27,540 --> 00:35:32,340
We need to take precautions before Aygül
works herself up.

280
00:35:34,740 --> 00:35:36,420
How?

281
00:35:36,420 --> 00:35:41,170
A proper marriage will bring
us and Aygül peace.

282
00:35:43,170 --> 00:35:45,510
What are you trying to say, Hatun?

283
00:35:46,580 --> 00:35:49,180
Who do you have in mind?

284
00:35:50,550 --> 00:35:52,980
Alişar Bey.

285
00:35:53,660 --> 00:35:57,020
Alişar Bey's Hatun passed away last year.

286
00:35:57,200 --> 00:36:00,800
I say we marry Alişar Bey to Aygül.

287
00:36:01,390 --> 00:36:05,490
When he came to the tent with
Sofia and Kalanoz today...

288
00:36:05,620 --> 00:36:08,580
I saw how Alişar Bey looked at Aygül.

289
00:36:10,360 --> 00:36:13,200
We should meet Alişar Bey
as soon as possible...

290
00:36:13,230 --> 00:36:16,180
and tell him about it.

291
00:36:18,650 --> 00:36:22,030
- Aygül...
- Can I come in, my Bey?

292
00:36:23,190 --> 00:36:24,730
Come in.

293
00:36:32,190 --> 00:36:35,540
What are you doing at this time of the night?

294
00:36:35,600 --> 00:36:36,840
My Bey...

295
00:36:37,070 --> 00:36:39,100
Sheikh Edebalı is in our tent.

296
00:36:45,160 --> 00:36:46,740
You should...

297
00:36:48,070 --> 00:36:50,660
have your eyes on him.

298
00:36:52,090 --> 00:36:56,090
- I'll know everything he does.
- Okay, my Bey.

299
00:37:03,980 --> 00:37:05,620
What will we do, my Bey?

300
00:37:11,750 --> 00:37:13,680
Edebalı is...

301
00:37:14,300 --> 00:37:15,710
trouble.

302
00:37:15,860 --> 00:37:20,070
It means that we'll take on...

303
00:37:20,130 --> 00:37:22,780
Mongols' rage and Seljuqs' doubt.

304
00:37:23,910 --> 00:37:27,910
I'm afraid that there's a connection...

305
00:37:28,680 --> 00:37:32,680
- between Osman and Edebalı.
- Won't you say something to him?

306
00:37:37,510 --> 00:37:39,670
No need to rush.

307
00:37:39,730 --> 00:37:42,150
Let him embrace his daughter.

308
00:37:42,360 --> 00:37:45,050
Let him settle.

309
00:37:45,890 --> 00:37:47,390
Don't forget...

310
00:37:47,780 --> 00:37:50,330
the hunt leaves a trace...

311
00:37:51,080 --> 00:37:53,250
and the hunter...

312
00:37:54,620 --> 00:37:56,450
traces.

313
00:38:04,930 --> 00:38:07,470
Our Mother Hacer was desperate too...

314
00:38:07,700 --> 00:38:09,210
because...

315
00:38:09,860 --> 00:38:14,680
the water that Prophet
İbrahim left to them...

316
00:38:15,460 --> 00:38:17,170
was run short.

317
00:38:18,030 --> 00:38:21,900
Our Mother Hacer who
worried about her son İsmail...

318
00:38:21,920 --> 00:38:25,920
dying of thirst in Mecca....

319
00:38:26,310 --> 00:38:29,450
started to seek for water...

320
00:38:29,860 --> 00:38:32,760
between Safa and Marwa.

321
00:38:33,400 --> 00:38:37,050
When she went for seven times...

322
00:38:38,380 --> 00:38:41,870
her son İsmail was exhausted.

323
00:38:42,210 --> 00:38:45,850
Thirst shook his little body.

324
00:38:46,730 --> 00:38:49,120
With the wisdom of Allah...

325
00:38:49,520 --> 00:38:51,660
she clicked his heels.

326
00:38:52,050 --> 00:38:54,690
Our Mother heard a voice then.

327
00:38:55,670 --> 00:38:59,670
She looked behind and saw that in the
place she left İsmail...

328
00:39:00,990 --> 00:39:03,980
there was water.

329
00:39:06,330 --> 00:39:08,510
Cebrail (a.s) created a water resource...

330
00:39:08,690 --> 00:39:10,990
after he saw the trouble...

331
00:39:11,330 --> 00:39:15,090
İsmal and Mother Hacer had been
going through...

332
00:39:15,500 --> 00:39:21,520
with the permission of Allah.

333
00:39:24,520 --> 00:39:28,230
They named it Zemzem.

334
00:39:30,140 --> 00:39:33,700
- It is healthy for Muslims, in sha Allah.
- In sha Allah.

335
00:39:34,860 --> 00:39:39,740
This will keep my daughter strong until
the cure arrives, in sha Allah.

336
00:39:51,760 --> 00:39:54,240
I wish Osman had never grown up.

337
00:39:55,880 --> 00:39:59,880
I wish he had been still a kid...

338
00:39:59,960 --> 00:40:01,980
not moving anywhere,
staying with you.

339
00:40:04,240 --> 00:40:06,340
Among all those troubles...

340
00:40:06,940 --> 00:40:09,970
being silent just to keep the tent safe...

341
00:40:12,190 --> 00:40:14,430
Annoys me, Hatun (lady).

342
00:40:14,720 --> 00:40:17,710
My Gündüz.
My Man.

343
00:40:17,850 --> 00:40:21,410
Everyone in the tent knows that you
are fair.

344
00:40:21,960 --> 00:40:24,080
Don't worry.

345
00:40:24,450 --> 00:40:25,960
This is Osman.

346
00:40:26,290 --> 00:40:29,200
He has always been zippy.

347
00:40:29,260 --> 00:40:32,610
Also, you know that he is brave.

348
00:40:33,290 --> 00:40:37,070
He can take care of himself.
Don't worry.

349
00:40:40,160 --> 00:40:41,990
No, Hatun. No.

350
00:40:43,280 --> 00:40:45,220
This time it is different.

351
00:40:45,730 --> 00:40:47,660
He is in great trouble.

352
00:40:49,590 --> 00:40:54,180
I fear that something bad will happen
to him.

353
00:40:56,220 --> 00:41:00,910
If he doesn't appear in the court tomorrow,
it means he accepts the provision.

354
00:41:02,330 --> 00:41:06,330
Everyone is tearing into him.

355
00:41:07,950 --> 00:41:11,670
You won't leave Osman alone, will you?

356
00:41:14,040 --> 00:41:15,420
Never.

357
00:41:17,700 --> 00:41:19,740
Even if he causes trouble...

358
00:41:20,280 --> 00:41:22,320
he is still my brother.

359
00:41:24,250 --> 00:41:26,330
My wolf-eyed brother.

360
00:41:28,080 --> 00:41:31,070
He is entrusted to me by my parents.

361
00:41:31,240 --> 00:41:32,410
Then...

362
00:41:33,230 --> 00:41:36,770
you need to take care of him.

363
00:41:37,990 --> 00:41:39,440
I took precautions.

364
00:41:41,910 --> 00:41:43,540
If something goes wrong...

365
00:41:44,170 --> 00:41:46,430
I'll abduct Osman.

366
00:41:48,110 --> 00:41:50,490
My uncle doesn't know.

367
00:41:52,730 --> 00:41:55,220
I can't let anyone get him.

368
00:41:55,890 --> 00:41:57,280
No one.

369
00:42:00,140 --> 00:42:02,260
People go away.

370
00:42:02,560 --> 00:42:03,870
Family stays.

371
00:42:04,160 --> 00:42:07,040
Family is permanent.

372
00:42:08,200 --> 00:42:11,260
This is what Gündüz Bey, the
grandchild of Süleyman Shah...

373
00:42:11,260 --> 00:42:13,470
Shah and son of Ertğrul Ghazi should do.

374
00:42:13,470 --> 00:42:16,510
May Allah open our way, my man.

375
00:42:16,660 --> 00:42:18,760
Amin, Hatun.

376
00:43:02,130 --> 00:43:03,490
Aybars!

377
00:43:06,160 --> 00:43:11,480
In sha Allah, I will take revenge for you,
my brother.

378
00:43:27,750 --> 00:43:29,570
What is happening here?

379
00:43:31,490 --> 00:43:33,420
Get out!

380
00:43:36,190 --> 00:43:38,120
Clumsy men!

381
00:43:52,320 --> 00:43:55,170
Why are you tiring yourself up, Princess?

382
00:43:56,510 --> 00:43:59,370
We need to be prepared for everything,
Commander.

383
00:44:01,400 --> 00:44:03,240
Did you take all the precautions?

384
00:44:03,800 --> 00:44:07,180
Don't worry, darling.
Everything is okay, but...

385
00:44:09,230 --> 00:44:11,230
I don't understand.

386
00:44:11,580 --> 00:44:13,850
Why is this treasure so important?

387
00:44:14,710 --> 00:44:18,050
Let us kill all the Ahis and Kayıs.

388
00:44:18,360 --> 00:44:20,970
We should finish this matter.

389
00:44:21,070 --> 00:44:23,230
If it was that easy...

390
00:44:23,310 --> 00:44:26,860
We would have finished it, Kalanoz.

391
00:44:26,930 --> 00:44:29,110
What is the hard thing here, Sofia?

392
00:44:29,450 --> 00:44:32,390
We have a strong army.

393
00:44:32,390 --> 00:44:37,300
Byzantine supports us.
We just need to declare a war.

394
00:44:43,210 --> 00:44:44,970
Those Turks...

395
00:44:45,390 --> 00:44:48,110
can't get on well with each other.

396
00:44:48,350 --> 00:44:51,180
But when someone from outside attacks
them...

397
00:44:51,180 --> 00:44:54,810
They stand together
and turn into a dragon.

398
00:44:58,930 --> 00:45:02,930
It was always like that, and this
will go on like that.

399
00:45:07,950 --> 00:45:09,980
But, don't worry.

400
00:45:09,980 --> 00:45:12,280
Master Yannis' intelligence make us...

401
00:45:12,660 --> 00:45:15,900
superior against them.

402
00:45:16,450 --> 00:45:19,270
I can't wait to capture Osman, but...

403
00:45:21,220 --> 00:45:22,910
This is Osman.

404
00:45:23,660 --> 00:45:26,390
Alişer Bey is involved too.

405
00:45:26,420 --> 00:45:29,460
Osman has to obey him.

406
00:45:30,200 --> 00:45:33,510
If he doesn't come, it will mean that
he accepts the provision.

407
00:45:34,930 --> 00:45:38,130
In that case, Alişar Bey will find him
before we do.

408
00:45:40,720 --> 00:45:44,010
The time has come.

409
00:45:44,010 --> 00:45:46,300
Let's go and get Osman.

410
00:45:56,040 --> 00:45:58,620
"I seek refuge in Allah from accursed Shaitan"

411
00:45:58,870 --> 00:46:01,060
"In the name of God, the Most
Gracious, the Most Merciful"

412
00:46:01,710 --> 00:46:03,450
By the racers, panting,

413
00:46:03,860 --> 00:46:05,830
"And the producers of sparks [when] striking

414
00:46:06,320 --> 00:46:08,320
And the chargers at dawn,"

415
00:46:09,110 --> 00:46:11,150
"Stirring up thereby [clouds of] dust,

416
00:46:11,540 --> 00:46:13,810
Arriving thereby in the center collectively,

417
00:46:14,270 --> 00:46:17,710
Indeed mankind, to his Lord, is ungrateful.

418
00:46:18,500 --> 00:46:21,710
And indeed, he is to that a witness.

419
00:46:22,220 --> 00:46:25,700
And indeed he is, in love of wealth, intense.

420
00:46:26,340 --> 00:46:30,440
But does he not know that when the contents of the graves are scattered

421
00:46:30,820 --> 00:46:33,530
And that within the breasts is obtained,

422
00:46:33,740 --> 00:46:37,650
Indeed, their Lord with them,
that Day, is [fully] Acquainted.

423
00:46:38,140 --> 00:46:40,520
"Allaah Almighty has spoken the truth"

424
00:46:40,830 --> 00:46:44,150
Recitator: İsmail Hakkı Ürün
Aka Samsa Çavuş

425
00:46:54,780 --> 00:46:58,530
My Bey, why are you tying the tail of
the horse?

426
00:47:02,670 --> 00:47:04,550
So that it can know.

427
00:47:05,350 --> 00:47:08,430
- So that it can know.
- Know what, my Bey?

428
00:47:08,650 --> 00:47:16,690
That this is a war and this tie will break
if there is death in the end.

429
00:47:16,870 --> 00:47:19,650
This is a tradition, son.

430
00:47:20,060 --> 00:47:28,190
We tie the tail of the horse so that
it can know that there is a war.

431
00:47:28,450 --> 00:47:33,210
If its owner is martyred...

432
00:47:33,470 --> 00:47:38,480
its tail is cut and be used as a plume.

433
00:47:38,490 --> 00:47:40,990
Eyvallah (thank you) my Bey.

434
00:48:02,480 --> 00:48:04,860
Ya Allah!

435
00:48:08,870 --> 00:48:13,840
This weapon is my brother Aybars'.

436
00:48:15,360 --> 00:48:21,920
If I can't take revenge for my brother
with this weapon today...

437
00:48:23,150 --> 00:48:26,920
May it stick into my heart.

438
00:48:27,250 --> 00:48:31,860
The shahada (martyrdom) day has come,
brothers!

439
00:48:31,980 --> 00:48:38,580
Today, we will send the enemy to hell!

440
00:48:39,030 --> 00:48:42,470
- Allah is the greatest!
- Allah is the greatest!

441
00:48:42,480 --> 00:48:46,770
- Allah is the greatest!
- Allah is the greatest!

442
00:48:46,810 --> 00:48:57,000
- Allah is the greatest!
- Allah is the greatest!

443
00:49:36,140 --> 00:49:39,710
- Protect Princess Sofia!
- Protect her!

444
00:49:44,600 --> 00:49:46,610
They are here.

445
00:50:11,210 --> 00:50:15,950
I was waiting you to see at the court,
Osman Bey.

446
00:50:16,360 --> 00:50:23,000
I decided to establish divine justice
here, Sofia.

447
00:50:27,460 --> 00:50:32,750
I guess I will be the judge of that court.

448
00:50:36,100 --> 00:50:38,620
Hunting time!

449
00:50:50,450 --> 00:50:52,650
He trapepd us!

450
00:51:16,450 --> 00:51:22,150
Bala Hatun will be killed because of you,
Osman Bey.

451
00:51:22,220 --> 00:51:24,580
Alps!

452
00:51:36,920 --> 00:51:39,640
From now on...

453
00:51:39,730 --> 00:51:43,620
I am the one to decide here!

454
00:51:47,920 --> 00:51:51,850
- Allah is eternal!
- Allah is eternal!

455
00:52:30,330 --> 00:52:33,110
I want Osman Alive!

456
00:52:37,110 --> 00:52:41,940
With our own Kadıs (Muslim Judge), we
set up a fair court, Dündar Bey.

457
00:52:42,040 --> 00:52:46,700
Whatever the consequences are, we'll
substitute the peace in Söğüt again.

458
00:52:46,810 --> 00:52:50,810
The peace that my brother
Ertuğrul Bey left when he went..

459
00:52:50,950 --> 00:52:53,910
was spoiled by Osman.

460
00:52:54,360 --> 00:52:57,610
Today, every problem
should be solved here.

461
00:52:57,900 --> 00:53:01,900
We'll reach the
freedom together, Alişar Bey.

462
00:53:03,290 --> 00:53:06,930
Don't worry, Dündar Bey. Let's go.

463
00:53:07,360 --> 00:53:09,440
Kadıs(muslim judge) are about to come.

464
00:53:23,500 --> 00:53:27,500
Deploy behind the Han. If something
goes wrong...

465
00:53:28,610 --> 00:53:30,590
we'll take Osman.

466
00:53:32,090 --> 00:53:33,260
Kılıçalp...

467
00:53:34,150 --> 00:53:38,230
Even if he's my uncle, I
won't give him Osman.

468
00:53:47,500 --> 00:53:48,790
Osman...

469
00:53:49,980 --> 00:53:52,740
You're entrusted to me by my mother.

470
00:53:53,300 --> 00:53:55,720
I won't let anyone take you.

471
00:56:19,090 --> 00:56:22,680
You'll die today!

472
00:56:47,720 --> 00:56:49,090
Inglorious.

473
00:57:00,010 --> 00:57:02,460
You'll get in trouble, Osman.

474
00:57:05,200 --> 00:57:08,970
With a word that came out
of your ominous mouth...

475
00:57:08,970 --> 00:57:11,310
you killed my son.

476
00:57:12,440 --> 00:57:15,520
The death will be haram
(bad for Islam) for me...

477
00:57:15,550 --> 00:57:18,890
if I don't cut your cruel tongue.

478
00:57:20,040 --> 00:57:21,650
I know about...

479
00:57:21,650 --> 00:57:26,330
every sword blow that cut
your son's body, Bamsı Bey.

480
00:57:29,290 --> 00:57:34,330
His death was as heavy as his pain.

481
00:57:55,600 --> 00:57:57,310
Don't, Bamsı Bey!

482
00:57:58,680 --> 00:58:00,150
Don't, Bamsı Bey!

483
