742
01:29:49,340 --> 01:29:52,680
No one could grow weary
of us." - Yunus Emre

743
01:31:05,150 --> 01:31:07,990
The old man that you gave
a present at the bazaar is

744
01:31:10,550 --> 01:31:13,290
Yannis who dressed up like a dervish.

745
01:31:18,540 --> 01:31:21,270
Prophet's people came.

746
01:31:22,530 --> 01:31:24,190
They did.

747
01:31:25,800 --> 01:31:28,770
They became the sign of end time.

748
01:31:29,820 --> 01:31:30,860
They did.

749
01:31:33,560 --> 01:31:38,880
Our nature gets fulled with death.

750
01:31:40,150 --> 01:31:41,250
It does.

751
01:31:42,840 --> 01:31:46,370
Many problems exist, friends.

752
01:31:51,640 --> 01:31:54,440
Your handicraft...

753
01:31:57,040 --> 01:31:59,440
I didn't want to leave it.

754
01:32:01,070 --> 01:32:03,460
I thought about their love and...

755
01:32:05,580 --> 01:32:08,480
I found solace in it.

756
01:32:12,430 --> 01:32:14,600
Even if I die like Aslı...

757
01:32:16,870 --> 01:32:18,600
I'll be fine.

758
01:32:19,480 --> 01:32:21,210
You're in my life.

759
01:32:23,370 --> 01:32:26,270
I won't let you go, Bala Hatun.

760
01:32:33,310 --> 01:32:35,230
As you say.

761
01:32:40,190 --> 01:32:42,580
Ask for me in marriage, from my father.

762
01:33:05,770 --> 01:33:07,880
If you let me...

763
01:33:08,840 --> 01:33:10,230
then...

764
01:33:11,240 --> 01:33:13,530
when my father returns, I'll do it.

765
01:33:55,190 --> 01:33:56,730
Excuse me.

766
01:35:03,310 --> 01:35:04,990
Can I come in, Osman Bey?

767
01:35:06,370 --> 01:35:07,740
Come in, Konur.

768
01:35:16,400 --> 01:35:17,760
What happened? Tell me.

769
01:35:20,970 --> 01:35:22,510
What's it?

770
01:35:23,210 --> 01:35:24,870
Dündar Bey...

771
01:35:24,960 --> 01:35:27,910
He not only caged our Alps (men)...

772
01:35:28,050 --> 01:35:31,880
but he also took their weapons.

773
01:35:38,040 --> 01:35:41,260
It's time to settle accounts
with Dündar Bey.

774
01:35:49,000 --> 01:35:53,000
So that we get rid of the troubles...

775
01:35:53,880 --> 01:35:56,880
we better clear up the tent.

776
01:35:58,640 --> 01:36:02,640
We haven't talked about the trade issue
for a long time.

777
01:36:02,670 --> 01:36:06,510
The new bazaar is recovering.
We need to...

778
01:36:07,110 --> 01:36:09,430
manufacture something in the carpet room.

779
01:36:09,480 --> 01:36:13,990
Don't worry about it, Dündar Bey.
Kayı's Hatuns (ladies) will do it.

780
01:36:14,100 --> 01:36:16,160
When the new bazaar recovers...

781
01:36:16,190 --> 01:36:20,050
Kayıs' goods will be the best-qualified
ones.

782
01:36:20,180 --> 01:36:22,890
- Elhamdülillah (Thanks Allah).
- Thank Allah.

783
01:36:23,110 --> 01:36:25,780
We got rid all of our problems.

784
01:36:25,930 --> 01:36:29,650
From now on, it is about our
passion.

785
01:36:30,910 --> 01:36:32,970
No, nephew. No.

786
01:36:34,570 --> 01:36:37,530
We didn't get rid all of our problems.

787
01:36:38,460 --> 01:36:42,170
I have an issue with Osman.

788
01:36:44,750 --> 01:36:48,060
This has gone beyond too much.

789
01:36:49,680 --> 01:36:55,980
I have no intention to lose this tent
because of Osman's immaturity, Gündüz.

790
01:36:56,860 --> 01:37:00,010
I really wonder, there has been a lot of
things.

791
01:37:00,590 --> 01:37:04,450
Hasn't he got something to tell his uncle
as an explanation?

792
01:37:04,860 --> 01:37:07,240
Not just an explanation!

793
01:37:09,460 --> 01:37:12,240
I also need to call you to account,
Dündar Bey!

794
01:37:15,790 --> 01:37:18,870
You caged my alps (men).

795
01:37:19,570 --> 01:37:23,920
I can explain this, Osman.

796
01:37:23,920 --> 01:37:28,080
But you need to explain my Batur's
situation

797
01:37:28,110 --> 01:37:31,490
I had an issue with Batur.

798
01:37:32,740 --> 01:37:35,750
I solved it.

799
01:37:37,950 --> 01:37:43,080
Now, free my alps.

800
01:37:44,030 --> 01:37:50,090
- Otherwise...
- Otherwise what, Osman?

801
01:37:57,500 --> 01:38:01,680
I will solve my problem with Batur
entirely.

802
01:38:02,560 --> 01:38:07,620
Uncle, you heard Kalanoz.
Osman has been proved to right.

803
01:38:07,620 --> 01:38:10,840
- We need to free the alps.
- Gündüz.

804
01:38:11,250 --> 01:38:16,060
Do not interfere.

805
01:38:16,060 --> 01:38:20,220
He is chasing revenge for Aybars!

806
01:38:20,230 --> 01:38:26,200
However, my son's blood is still fresh!

807
01:38:27,650 --> 01:38:30,180
Your son has paid his treason.

808
01:38:30,180 --> 01:38:34,420
Osman, Uncle!
Enough!

809
01:38:34,500 --> 01:38:36,960
Enough already!

810
01:38:42,880 --> 01:38:47,630
Osman. Look.

811
01:38:47,870 --> 01:38:51,340
Your brother is on your side.

812
01:38:53,240 --> 01:38:57,250
Gündüz was involved in that, too.

813
01:38:57,970 --> 01:39:02,830
So, will you betray us?

814
01:39:10,350 --> 01:39:15,640
Blood for blood.
Don't you know that?

815
01:39:16,710 --> 01:39:18,860
Uncle!

816
01:39:21,200 --> 01:39:24,060
If you want blood...

817
01:39:24,920 --> 01:39:27,710
here you go.

818
01:40:45,000 --> 01:40:48,240
I knew you weren't going to betray me,
Kalanoz.

819
01:40:48,240 --> 01:40:51,260
There was no other way to save you,
Sofia.

820
01:40:53,100 --> 01:40:55,390
So, it was a game.

821
01:40:55,490 --> 01:41:00,670
We have grand ideas that tie us together.

822
01:41:01,150 --> 01:41:04,470
Not just our ideals.

823
01:41:09,740 --> 01:41:14,940
Did you request for this execution?

824
01:41:14,950 --> 01:41:18,160
Yes, my daughter.
I'll die.

825
01:41:18,450 --> 01:41:22,370
I need to be executed in front of Osman
and others' eyes.

826
01:41:22,400 --> 01:41:28,630
I will never let this happen.
They need to kill me first.

827
01:41:29,320 --> 01:41:34,370
The first thing that they taught us in the
Margarıt Abbey was that...

828
01:41:35,060 --> 01:41:38,790
You can't live without dying, Sofia.

829
01:42:00,200 --> 01:42:05,480
- Osman.
- How can you do this to yourself, Osman?

830
01:42:09,870 --> 01:42:12,660
Why are you so sad, Aygül?

831
01:42:12,730 --> 01:42:17,220
Haven't you seen Osman, mother?
He stabbed himself!

832
01:42:17,240 --> 01:42:22,920
Don't you have honor?

833
01:42:23,270 --> 01:42:26,980
You are Dündar Bey's daughter, Aygül Hatun.

834
01:42:27,050 --> 01:42:30,810
Why are you crying?
Pull yourself together!

835
01:42:30,830 --> 01:42:36,040
-Mother...
-If you go on crying, don't call me mother again.

836
01:42:36,060 --> 01:42:39,680
Mother, what are you talking about?
I...

837
01:42:39,680 --> 01:42:43,510
You are crying for Osman, who
killed your brother...

838
01:42:43,570 --> 01:42:48,490
and disobeyed your father, your Bey.
You are crying for Osman!

839
01:42:50,690 --> 01:42:54,810
Get out of this tent and you'll see.

840
01:42:54,840 --> 01:43:00,870
He organised everybody.
He is rebelling against his uncle.

841
01:43:01,150 --> 01:43:03,530
And you cry for him, ha?

842
01:43:03,570 --> 01:43:06,470
- Mother, look...
- Shut up!

843
01:43:06,500 --> 01:43:10,780
You should be ashamed of yourself
as a Kayı.

844
01:43:16,420 --> 01:43:22,460
Look, daughter. You need to marry a
strong Bey.

845
01:43:22,460 --> 01:43:27,130
You'll marry a strong Bey and make
your father stronger.

846
01:43:27,130 --> 01:43:31,770
I am not talking about a random Bey
or his son, I mean the Bannerlord.

847
01:43:34,500 --> 01:43:38,290
- You'll marry Alişar Bey, Aygül.
- Mother, I prefer dying.

848
01:43:38,300 --> 01:43:43,740
- I prefer dying, mother!
- That's all I have to say, Aygül.

849
01:43:43,780 --> 01:43:46,240
You shall not speak.

850
01:43:46,310 --> 01:43:51,780
If you don't do what I say, you are
dead to me.

851
01:44:02,110 --> 01:44:05,930
Osman has proved his braveness, father.

852
01:44:05,950 --> 01:44:12,530
Yes, my Sheikh. If it wasn't for him,
neither Bala Hatun nor Tursun would live.

853
01:44:15,980 --> 01:44:21,760
The one who puts braveness and faith
into hearts...

854
01:44:22,180 --> 01:44:24,630
is Allah.

855
01:44:25,790 --> 01:44:27,900
As to Osman...

856
01:44:28,450 --> 01:44:32,840
he is a rookie for now.

857
01:44:32,840 --> 01:44:37,150
If he is disciplined well...

858
01:44:37,810 --> 01:44:42,940
and trained well, he will be a
sharp sword.

859
01:44:43,740 --> 01:44:47,280
If not...

860
01:44:47,640 --> 01:44:50,280
he will be just a piece of iron.

861
01:44:56,770 --> 01:44:58,450
Osman.

862
01:45:09,960 --> 01:45:13,550
Osman Bey, what happened to you?

863
01:45:17,930 --> 01:45:21,230
I punished myself.

864
01:45:21,730 --> 01:45:24,640
Don't worry, Edebali.

865
01:45:26,220 --> 01:45:28,920
Did you stab yourself?

866
01:45:29,370 --> 01:45:31,850
The dagger fastened on my body.

867
01:45:32,300 --> 01:45:37,160
However, the blood is Dündar Bey's.

868
01:45:44,230 --> 01:45:46,420
Remember that...

869
01:45:47,340 --> 01:45:50,350
Wounds can heal.

870
01:45:50,970 --> 01:45:54,390
But the grudge doesn't go away.

871
01:46:12,590 --> 01:46:15,280
Rest here.

872
01:46:16,260 --> 01:46:19,740
- I will go to the Alp Tent.
- Eyvallah (okay) Osman Bey.

873
01:46:19,870 --> 01:46:21,930
Eyvallah (okay).

874
01:46:34,720 --> 01:46:37,640
Drain the blood.

875
01:46:37,850 --> 01:46:41,890
I'll set up a fire.
We need to brand the wound.

876
01:46:58,310 --> 01:46:59,890
May peace be upon you.

877
01:47:00,390 --> 01:47:02,140
And peace be upon you, too.

878
01:47:29,770 --> 01:47:31,880
Boran, son.

879
01:47:36,430 --> 01:47:38,210
Son, what happened?

880
01:47:39,150 --> 01:47:41,670
It's nothing important, Bamsı Bey.

881
01:47:50,220 --> 01:47:54,160
If there's nothing important, then
what are those scars, brother Boran?

882
01:47:55,460 --> 01:47:57,440
Who did this to you?

883
01:48:04,130 --> 01:48:06,830
Who did this to you?

884
01:48:09,280 --> 01:48:12,960
Batur came here, Konuralp,
then this happened.

885
01:48:13,120 --> 01:48:16,970
How quickly did Batur
forget about his knife wound!

886
01:48:17,290 --> 01:48:20,160
I will deal with him now.

887
01:48:20,240 --> 01:48:24,080
Samsa Bey, don't let what
happened here be heard outside.

888
01:48:24,960 --> 01:48:29,210
Osman Bey is busy with his own troubles,
don't let us trouble him too.

889
01:48:29,980 --> 01:48:34,180
Sergeant Samsa, Boran Alp is right.

890
01:48:35,500 --> 01:48:38,470
Now is not the right time.

891
01:48:42,130 --> 01:48:44,580
If not today, then tomorrow...

892
01:48:45,060 --> 01:48:47,830
... if not tomorrow, then later.

893
01:48:48,360 --> 01:48:51,070
Spilled blood won't go without
punishment, brother Boran.

894
01:48:51,220 --> 01:48:56,680
You will not get away with this Batur.
You will not get away with this.

895
01:48:58,740 --> 01:49:01,270
Today, we have lost blood.

896
01:49:01,840 --> 01:49:05,550
But when the time comes,
we will spill their blood.

897
01:49:25,170 --> 01:49:27,160
Thank you, brother.

898
01:49:27,520 --> 01:49:28,650
Thank you.

899
01:49:38,400 --> 01:49:42,400
My Osman, my brother.

900
01:49:43,890 --> 01:49:46,380
When will you stop bleeding?

901
01:49:48,220 --> 01:49:50,090
Look at you.

902
01:49:51,810 --> 01:49:54,900
There is more blood
to be spilled, brother.

903
01:49:55,560 --> 01:49:57,820
There is more blood to be spilled.

904
01:50:31,150 --> 01:50:33,230
"In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful"

905
01:50:35,770 --> 01:50:37,860
Like you said, brother...

906
01:50:38,720 --> 01:50:42,720
Valiants take matters
into their own hands.

907
01:50:53,930 --> 01:50:56,790
"In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful"

908
01:51:33,380 --> 01:51:34,560
Erkut Alp.

909
01:51:35,060 --> 01:51:39,060
You should go take a look and
find out where Osman Bey is.

910
01:51:39,670 --> 01:51:40,880
Yes, my Bey.

911
01:51:56,000 --> 01:52:00,500
Erkut Alp is two feet tall.
One foot is just stomach.

912
01:52:03,480 --> 01:52:08,130
You say two feet tall, brother Konur,
but there's more than that.

913
01:52:11,340 --> 01:52:17,370
I know, brother Boran, I know. When I say
two feet, another one is just his heart.

914
01:52:18,840 --> 01:52:19,960
You are right.

915
01:52:21,530 --> 01:52:26,490
When we arrived at the Tent, you gave your
hide to Osman Bey, and your tent to me.

916
01:52:26,790 --> 01:52:33,680
Now, you are my guest in my tent, I won't let
you go anywhere tonight, Sergeant Samsa.

917
01:52:38,480 --> 01:52:42,530
Thank you, Konur Alp, I'm not
intending to go anywhere either.

918
01:52:43,940 --> 01:52:46,170
Mashallah, valiants.

919
01:52:49,620 --> 01:52:54,150
What is it, Erkut, were you scared
because we might eat your share too?

920
01:52:58,810 --> 01:53:00,460
What is it?

921
01:53:04,910 --> 01:53:07,300
Okay, you should sit.

922
01:53:17,350 --> 01:53:19,580
What is it, Bamsı Bey?

923
01:53:20,400 --> 01:53:25,490
Sons, my Osman is
apparently busy right now.

924
01:53:26,380 --> 01:53:31,620
But cancelling a table is against
the traditions of valiants.

925
01:53:32,060 --> 01:53:36,190
So, let's start then, come on.

926
01:53:36,440 --> 01:53:39,740
Come on, Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.

927
01:53:40,720 --> 01:53:44,720
- Here, son.
- Thank you, my Bey. Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.

928
01:54:16,920 --> 01:54:20,140
Would a daughter of Bey
cry like this, Aygül Hatun?

929
01:54:21,360 --> 01:54:24,480
I'm not with Osman while he is bleeding.

930
01:54:24,570 --> 01:54:27,150
Then go! Go to his side!

931
01:54:27,660 --> 01:54:31,360
He spilled your brother's blood.
He will also drain your tears, go!

932
01:54:31,470 --> 01:54:36,740
Burçin, that's enough,
don't be so hard on me!

933
01:54:37,000 --> 01:54:38,910
That's enough, I'm begging you!

934
01:54:39,050 --> 01:54:44,560
Your eyes are blind except to Osman,
but Osman's eyes can only see Bala.

935
01:54:45,940 --> 01:54:50,650
I have never loved anyone
but Osman in my life, Burçin.

936
01:54:50,770 --> 01:54:55,350
Then what, Aygül, have you ever
heard any good words in your life?

937
01:54:55,640 --> 01:55:01,060
Have you ever seen a smile, tell me, was
it worth the tears you've dropped for him?

938
01:55:01,420 --> 01:55:03,330
Was it worth it, Aygül?

939
01:55:08,200 --> 01:55:10,060
My Allah...

940
01:55:11,170 --> 01:55:13,440
... give me the strength to be patient.

941
01:55:14,400 --> 01:55:18,640
Or just take my life, I'm begging you.

942
01:55:19,170 --> 01:55:21,560
Take it so I will be relieved.

943
01:55:36,460 --> 01:55:37,950
Osman Bey.

944
01:55:42,780 --> 01:55:47,710
You honored us, welcomed
us in your father's Tent.

945
01:55:48,710 --> 01:55:54,530
If Gündüz Bey allows me to, I would
want to speak a few words to you.

946
01:56:18,500 --> 01:56:24,500
Friends informed me, you cut
someone's hand in the bazaar.

947
01:56:25,120 --> 01:56:29,450
- It was a thief.
- Now you've hurt yourself.

948
01:56:30,030 --> 01:56:34,600
- I punished myself.
- Are you the justice, Osman Bey?

949
01:56:34,740 --> 01:56:36,650
If that's necessary, then I am!

950
01:56:40,520 --> 01:56:42,150
Do you really think...

951
01:56:42,820 --> 01:56:46,970
... justice is secured by brute
force and a black weapon?

952
01:56:47,540 --> 01:56:51,640
What can overcome injustice
but a black weapon, Edebali?

953
01:56:51,900 --> 01:56:53,580
Justice can.

954
01:56:55,440 --> 01:57:00,060
Justice needs the ability to see
a white hair in white milk...

955
01:57:01,010 --> 01:57:05,680
... and the ability to see a
black snake on a black rock.

956
01:57:06,620 --> 01:57:12,390
Justice does not only needs a strong
arm and a black weapon...

957
01:57:13,050 --> 01:57:16,790
... it also needs foresight, and insight.

958
01:57:18,810 --> 01:57:27,300
His holiness, Usame once killed a man who recited
the kalima shahadah and asked for mercy.

959
01:57:28,100 --> 01:57:32,470
Our Prophet called Usame.

960
01:57:32,750 --> 01:57:38,840
He said, "Did you kill a man who
has announced his faith?"

961
01:57:40,900 --> 01:57:45,180
When Usame defended himself by saying
"He said the words because he was scared."...

962
01:57:46,000 --> 01:57:48,830
Our benevolent Prophet said...

963
01:57:49,030 --> 01:57:56,110
" Did you open his heart out to speak
so sure about his intentions, his feelings?"

964
01:57:59,400 --> 01:58:00,620
Osman Bey.

965
01:58:01,820 --> 01:58:04,540
Is it right to do as you please...

966
01:58:05,380 --> 01:58:09,480
... without even asking, consulting...

967
01:58:10,230 --> 01:58:14,440
... thinking thoroughly about
it, even if it was a thief?

968
01:58:18,490 --> 01:58:23,110
Where is the kadi?
Where are the witnesses?

969
01:58:23,420 --> 01:58:25,030
Where is the trial?

970
01:58:27,480 --> 01:58:31,740
You judge by yourself,
and decide by yourself.

971
01:58:32,180 --> 01:58:37,200
And we are not skilled enough
to read people's hearts.

972
01:58:38,210 --> 01:58:45,370
If we have a talent like this, then we
should first read our own hearts.

973
01:58:50,600 --> 01:58:54,890
Now, let's talk about your bleeding wound.

974
01:58:56,820 --> 01:59:01,410
While Our Prophet Muhammad,
Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam (PBUH) even warned...

975
01:59:03,260 --> 01:59:07,890
... Ebu'd- Derda, who was harming
his body by keeping himself...

976
01:59:08,440 --> 01:59:12,440
... from all the world's
flavours by saying...

977
01:59:12,830 --> 01:59:19,520
... " Your soul is your
wrist, treat it well."...

978
01:59:20,020 --> 01:59:25,690
... would it be right to harm
yourself, stab yourself?

979
01:59:30,740 --> 01:59:38,470
Osman, blazing like a flash in the pan.

980
01:59:41,970 --> 01:59:43,950
Little Osman.

981
01:59:45,710 --> 01:59:48,770
We say " When you walk,
let the justice walk with you...

982
01:59:49,620 --> 01:59:53,370
..." when you smile, let the
mercy smile with you...

983
01:59:53,630 --> 01:59:57,920
..." when you endure tyranny,
let the patience stand up for you...

984
01:59:58,260 --> 02:00:02,580
..." and let the people see
the government in you."

985
02:00:03,250 --> 02:00:05,840
But look at what you do.

986
02:00:13,240 --> 02:00:17,480
Naive Osman, little Osman.

987
02:00:18,060 --> 02:00:22,790
A swift person hardly ever
gets a job done right.

988
02:00:24,970 --> 02:00:27,370
You should know it like this.

989
02:00:57,860 --> 02:01:03,270
Son, Boran. A horse has strong feet,
a bard has an agile tongue.

990
02:01:03,590 --> 02:01:09,900
May neither our adhans nor our bards be
silenced. Come on, sing a song for us.

991
02:01:12,780 --> 02:01:17,120
A bard with a dombra has words,
a Bey has his commands.

992
02:01:18,600 --> 02:01:21,460
Will it be a mournful or a
cheerful one, my Bamsı Bey?

993
02:01:24,000 --> 02:01:28,620
Son, it should neither be
a mournful, or a cheerful one.

994
02:01:29,770 --> 02:01:33,770
May it has wisdom. May it has wisdom, son.

995
02:01:34,430 --> 02:01:40,140
My Ertuğrul Bey loved how you sing
"Sevda-yı Muhammed".

996
02:01:41,800 --> 02:01:45,470
- Sing us that.
- Thank you, my Bey.

997
02:01:52,500 --> 02:01:58,490
Then let's be with the Great Yesevi,
the sage of Turkistan.

998
02:01:59,000 --> 02:02:05,810
Yes, yes, let us be with him so that our
hearts can be filled with his wisdom, son.

999
02:02:06,220 --> 02:02:07,760
Thank you.

1000
02:02:14,340 --> 02:02:19,040
"Sevda-yı Muhammed", from Hoca Ahmet Yesevi

1001
02:02:19,290 --> 02:02:47,100
Love of Muhammed happened to me.

1002
02:02:47,320 --> 02:03:11,420
That is why I am devoted to Muhammed.

1003
02:03:13,860 --> 02:03:19,080
Love of Muhammed happened to me.

1004
02:03:19,400 --> 02:03:24,050
That is why I am devoted to Muhammed.

1005
02:03:24,360 --> 02:03:29,580
One with an ummah is always grateful.

1006
02:03:30,080 --> 02:03:35,010
Then, my Allah, let me
be a devotee of Muhammed.

1007
02:03:40,900 --> 02:03:46,160
Allah gave me the love of Muhammed.

1008
02:03:46,280 --> 02:03:51,080
Let me be a devotee of just Muhammed.

1009
02:03:51,830 --> 02:03:56,380
Love of Muhammed happened to me.

1010
02:03:56,770 --> 02:04:02,120
That is why I am devoted to Muhammed.

1011
02:04:07,730 --> 02:04:12,570
Making me go through the
whole universe like Mecnun.

1012
02:04:13,050 --> 02:04:18,810
Making me go crazy for Muhammed.

1013
02:04:23,640 --> 02:04:28,710
He's never eaten food, but always sorrow.

1014
02:04:29,220 --> 02:04:34,180
You are the miracle of Muhammed's sorrow.

1015
02:04:34,750 --> 02:04:39,670
Love of Muhammed happened to me.

1016
02:04:39,820 --> 02:04:45,090
That is why I am devoted to Muhammed.

1017
02:04:56,000 --> 02:05:01,320
Shah of shahs asked for ummah's sins.

1018
02:05:01,690 --> 02:05:06,520
There is no fear in us in the
judgment day because of Muhammed.

1019
02:05:12,090 --> 02:05:17,570
Let me fly away with your grace, Allah.

1020
02:05:17,630 --> 02:05:23,080
Give me a drop of Muhammed's sea.

1021
02:05:23,210 --> 02:05:28,030
Love of Muhammed happened to me.

1022
02:05:28,200 --> 02:05:33,560
That is why I am devoted to Muhammed.

1023
02:05:44,310 --> 02:05:49,720
Let your dark face meet Pir-i Kamil's feet.

1024
02:05:49,920 --> 02:05:55,460
If He pleases, he would
allow us to see Muhammed.

1025
02:06:00,630 --> 02:06:05,600
This poor Yesevi wants to
see The Holy Chamber.

1026
02:06:05,630 --> 02:06:10,810
Would it be possible to
reach his feet's dirt?

1027
02:06:11,340 --> 02:06:16,270
Love of Muhammed happened to me.

1028
02:06:16,680 --> 02:06:21,660
That is why I am devoted to Muhammed.

1029
02:06:21,950 --> 02:06:26,960
Love of Muhammed happened to me.

1030
02:06:27,120 --> 02:06:32,810
That is why I am devoted to Muhammed.

1031
02:06:35,580 --> 02:06:38,400
- MashAllah, my valiant.
- Thank you, my Bey.

1032
02:06:42,020 --> 02:06:44,510
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.

1033
02:06:46,990 --> 02:06:49,260
My Allah...

1034
02:06:49,850 --> 02:06:56,280
... our love, fight or even intentions...

1035
02:06:57,690 --> 02:06:59,770
... are of Muhammed(saw)'s.

1036
02:07:02,700 --> 02:07:07,330
He is the warrior we
obey from all eternity.

1037
02:07:08,620 --> 02:07:15,280
We go to the battlefields with his name,
and be victorious with his name.

1038
02:07:17,400 --> 02:07:22,610
My Allah, we forged
His name on our hearts...

1039
02:07:23,320 --> 02:07:29,700
We forged His name on our efforts,
we forged His name on our eyes.

1040
02:07:30,320 --> 02:07:36,150
My Allah, don't let our
efforts be without His wish.

1041
02:07:36,350 --> 02:07:37,610
Amin.

1042
02:07:38,390 --> 02:07:46,060
My Allah, if we are hungry, we will
be satiated with His name.

1043
02:07:47,090 --> 02:07:52,080
If we are naked, we will
put on his love for us.

1044
02:07:52,410 --> 02:07:57,670
If we die, we will live with his cause.

1045
02:08:00,060 --> 02:08:06,630
My Allah, he is our beloved.
The blood we spill is for him...

1046
02:08:07,190 --> 02:08:12,860
... the glory we take, the reputation
we have, all of these are for him.

1047
02:08:14,210 --> 02:08:22,920
My Allah, don't let us and our
descendants stray from his way.

1048
02:08:23,000 --> 02:08:24,150
Amin.

1049
02:08:24,590 --> 02:08:30,560
Because friends of Ertuğrul
Gazi can't be without him.

1050
02:08:32,670 --> 02:08:37,290
They would give their lives,
but not their beloved.

1051
02:09:16,270 --> 02:09:19,250
I will marry you when
my father comes back.

1052
02:09:57,150 --> 02:09:59,080
Welcome, Aygül Hatun.

1053
02:09:59,450 --> 02:10:05,080
This is my uncle's Tent, you came here,
but you are not welcome here, you should know that.

1054
02:10:05,970 --> 02:10:11,460
Many of your friends died in the bazaar but you
are looking at a plate and smiling, Hatun.

1055
02:10:15,700 --> 02:10:17,290
Tell me.

1056
02:10:19,830 --> 02:10:22,340
What is the secret you are keeping?

1057
02:10:26,500 --> 02:10:31,800
Our friends died, may Allah
have mercy on their souls.

1058
02:10:34,620 --> 02:10:38,680
But you know, I also barely saved my life.

1059
02:10:38,750 --> 02:10:42,750
Ever since you came to our Tent,
we are cursed with troubles.

1060
02:10:44,340 --> 02:10:47,990
I know very well that death
is walking with you, Hatun.

1061
02:10:48,850 --> 02:10:53,000
One who says "I know.",
doesn't know anything.

1062
02:10:55,480 --> 02:10:58,690
And we don't intend to
make anyone uncomfortable.

1063
02:10:58,870 --> 02:11:03,000
You say you don't
intend to, but you do.

1064
02:11:03,810 --> 02:11:05,490
And Osman...

1065
02:11:07,610 --> 02:11:10,700
... Osman is always in trouble.

1066
02:11:13,060 --> 02:11:20,160
First, he lost his blood brother,
then he stabbed my brother because of you.

1067
02:11:20,840 --> 02:11:23,740
Now he spilled his own blood.

1068
02:11:26,210 --> 02:11:29,030
Get your hands off Osman.

1069
02:11:30,350 --> 02:11:34,720
You share the same blood,
you grew up together...

1070
02:11:35,920 --> 02:11:39,890
... but you haven't been
able to know Osman, Hatun.

1071
02:11:42,610 --> 02:11:47,170
Osman is not a valiant that
can be held, or be pushed away.

1072
02:11:49,360 --> 02:11:55,260
Whatever he's done, he's done
with his own courage, own will.

1073
02:12:02,070 --> 02:12:08,430
You clearly came here filled with anger,
you don't speak about good, but only bad.

1074
02:12:09,160 --> 02:12:15,030
If you don't have anything
else to say, leave me alone.

1075
02:12:15,680 --> 02:12:24,530
I have said what I needed to say. Now, take the
curse you brought with yourselves, and begone!

1076
02:13:44,960 --> 02:13:49,740
I've looked everywhere in the Tent,
my Bey, neither Edebali or Bala Hatun is here.

1077
02:13:50,510 --> 02:13:55,060
- Tursun.
- I've also checked medics, Tursun is gone too.

1078
02:14:01,670 --> 02:14:06,800
Send word to the Valiants, they should
prepare, we are going to the New Bazaar.

1079
02:14:19,560 --> 02:14:21,800
I've brought you a meal.

1080
02:14:22,800 --> 02:14:26,800
Thank you Aygül Hatun,
I need to go quickly.

1081
02:14:30,230 --> 02:14:32,290
Are you going after that Hatun?

1082
02:14:33,080 --> 02:14:36,400
I would want to know why
did they leave without a word.

1083
02:14:37,940 --> 02:14:39,730
Don't go, Osman.

1084
02:14:42,520 --> 02:14:46,520
You went after her for once,
and we were drowned in troubles.

1085
02:14:47,000 --> 02:14:51,450
- What are you saying, Aygül Hatun?
- That Hatun is cursed.

1086
02:14:52,780 --> 02:14:55,300
She won't be good for you.

1087
02:14:56,690 --> 02:14:59,550
Everything that happened
to us is because of her.

1088
02:14:59,970 --> 02:15:06,110
Everything that happened to us is because of
your father and your brother's arrogance, Aygül Hatun.

1089
02:15:08,630 --> 02:15:10,600
You should know it like this.

1090
02:16:03,570 --> 02:16:05,410
Wait for me here.

1091
02:17:10,380 --> 02:17:12,090
Edebali.

1092
02:18:23,620 --> 02:18:25,540
I've never seen my Bey like this before.

1093
02:18:25,680 --> 02:18:30,660
When he couldn't see Edebalı and Tursun
in the Tent, Osman Bey lost himself.

1094
02:18:32,750 --> 02:18:36,220
- Not because of this.
- Then why?

1095
02:18:36,440 --> 02:18:40,800
Osman Bey lost himself when
he couldn't find Bala Hatun.

1096
02:18:44,850 --> 02:18:46,200
I know.

1097
02:18:48,160 --> 02:18:50,080
This is love.

1098
02:18:54,840 --> 02:18:58,470
Osman Bey's heart is
burning with love's fire.

1099
02:19:06,510 --> 02:19:08,160
Samsa Bey...

1100
02:19:10,050 --> 02:19:12,130
... what do you know about love?

1101
02:19:12,970 --> 02:19:17,340
Haven't you found love
in battles, in fighting?

1102
02:19:23,780 --> 02:19:29,670
Weren't you married with
your weapon, Sergeant Samsa?

1103
02:19:35,790 --> 02:19:43,880
What happened, your eyes look cloudy,
your heart is darkened, tell us?

1104
02:19:46,620 --> 02:19:49,640
What makes you wander
into the emptiness, my Bey?

1105
02:19:50,660 --> 02:19:54,010
Don't rip my heart,
or I will rip your corpses.

1106
02:20:13,850 --> 02:20:18,900
Sergeant Samsa, we are
brothers-in-arms with you now.

1107
02:20:19,460 --> 02:20:22,750
Didn't we go to the
infidel's place together?

1108
02:20:22,970 --> 02:20:26,420
Didn't we spill infidel's
blood together?

1109
02:20:26,790 --> 02:20:32,200
There are no secrets between
us from now on, tell us.

1110
02:20:33,990 --> 02:20:36,570
I am worried about Osman Bey.

1111
02:20:37,830 --> 02:20:39,740
Why is that, Samsa Bey?

1112
02:20:45,260 --> 02:20:51,060
Love, Boran Alp, blinds Beyhood
of Beys, blunts weapons of the valiants.

1113
02:20:53,050 --> 02:20:54,990
How do you know that?

1114
02:20:58,730 --> 02:21:05,600
Have your heart burnt with
love's fire before, Sergeant Samsa?

1115
02:21:09,960 --> 02:21:11,910
Burning would be too easy.

1116
02:21:13,510 --> 02:21:17,000
Then tell us, we are your brothers.

1117
02:21:18,460 --> 02:21:20,410
Mind your own business!

1118
02:21:52,670 --> 02:21:59,100
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com